
                                  SYSOP EDITOR
   FOR VERSION 6.x of SE          ------------
   INCOMPATIBLE WITH PREVIOUS
   RELEASES

  I.  Classification

    Warning, this document is highly classified.  The Classification level
 of this document is "SYSOP EYES ONLY".  If you do not have the security
 level of "SYSOP", then you must by law of the interplanetary government,
 not read the following information.

 II.  Startup

    To start the sysop editor, you must place it in the directory with
 the game files.  After you do this, it is all set up.  Next move to that
 directory and type the following, "sysedit".  That is all there is to it!

III.  Using the Sysop Editor

    The sysop editor is set up in a series of menus.  Each provides you
 with several options.  To view the menu of options type a "?".  To access
 one of the menu options type in the letter or number for that item.

     A.  Main Menu

    The main menu is a top level menu of your options.  You only have a few
 choices from here, but each leads into a more detail menu.  The options
 from here are as follows:

      (A)lliance Menu       --  A menu where you can view and change the
                               names of the various alliances in the
                               Universe.  NOTE: You can't change the amount
                               of forces in the alliance from here, but
                               instead you must do it from the player menu.

      (P)layer Menu         --  The main use of this program is done in this
                               menu.  This will allow you to edit and modify
                               almost every value in the game.

      (Q)uit                --  Just what it says, quit.  It will ask you if
                               you wish to save the changes you have made
                               during that session.

     B.  Alliance Menu

    This is a simple menu that will allow you to list, view, and change the
 names of the alliances.  The following options are available:

      (L)ist Alliances       --  This will list all the alliances.

      (D)issolve Alliance     --  This will dissolve an alliance.

      (C)hange Alliance Name --  This will allow you to change the name of
                                an alliance.

      (Q)uit                 --  Quit and return to the main menu.

     C.  Player Menu

    This is by far the second most complicated menu.  It will give you various
 options including:

      (L)ist Players          --  This will list all the players.

      (R)emove Player         --  Use this in order to kill an empire.

      (M)odify Player         --  Leads you to the most complicated menu
                                 in the sysop editor.  The main reason
                                 for writing this document.

      (Q)uit                  --  Again, Quits and returns to main menu.

     D.  Modify Player Menu

    This menu isn't really hard to use, and is actually quite simple.  The
 reason I need to do a write up on it is because in order to save screen
 space, I have used several abbreviations, that might not jump right to mind.
 Most of them are acronyms.

        ID         -  Inactive Days
        SLD        -  Space Lord Days
        PS         -  Plague Status
        IA         -  Intelligence Agents (AKA - Covert Agents)
        TM         -  Troop Morale
        S          -  Soldiers
        F          -  Fighters
        HC         -  Heavy Cruisers
        DS         -  Defense Stations
        TS         -  Team Soldiers
        TDS        -  Team Defense Stations
        THC        -  Team Heavy Cruisers
        US         -  Used Soldiers
        UF         -  Used Fighters
        UHC        -  Used Heavy Cruisers
        UIA        -  Used Intelligence Agents
FP, OP, DP, and GP -  Planets  (Food, Ore, Defense, and Government)

    Those are the list of terms.  Next you get a menu.  I will not say much
 about them because they are basically self-explanatory.  Some like "Military"
 are sub-menus.  Be warned, that if you give someone protection that has more
 planets than the maximum for protection, it will be taken away on their
 first turn.  Also things like PS (plague status) have maximum values.  The
 sysop editor will allow you to enter illegal ones.  But the Space Empire
 itself will correct them.

 IV.  Save Files?

    If for some reason you make a mistake and you can't remember the old value,
 just exit the sysop editor.  It will ask you if you wish to save the files.
 Answer "NO" and the sysop editor will not save the files.

